// Test: Tuple type basic usage
// Spec: 03-TYPES.md § 4.3 Tuple Types
// Priority: P0 - Bootstrap Critical
//
// KNOWN FAILURE: Tuple Indexing
// sigil2 doesn't support tuple indexing (t.0, t.1, etc.)
// Outputs "null" instead of tuple element.
//
// Purpose:
// Validate tuple type construction and access.
//
// Expected behavior:
// Should print 42 (first element of tuple)

rite main() {
    ≔ t: !(i32, i32) = (42, 99);
    println(t.0);
}
